{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 2590,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The earth receives about 90 petajoules of\nenergy from the sun every second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6850,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That’s a lot – enough to satisfy all human\nenergy needs thousands of times over."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11550,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, the earth also radiates an equal\namount of energy back into space as heat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15960,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(An almost equal amount, anyway -- the Earth\nis gradually heating up, but that's another"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19320,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "story.)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20320,
    "dDurationMs": 4710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if energy in equals energy out, how can\nwe possibly be using any energy to do anything?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25030,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What matters, it turns out, isn’t simply\nenergy – it’s useful energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28790,
    "dDurationMs": 4210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And energy is useful when it comes packaged\nin a low-entropy form."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33000,
    "dDurationMs": 4730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The total amount of energy in any closed system\ncan’t change, of course -- energy is conserved."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37730,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that energy can be in different states\nof usefulness."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40790,
    "dDurationMs": 4010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There is useful energy in the water behind\na dam, which will flow until the level is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44800,
    "dDurationMs": 2950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the same on both sides, but will never go\nback “up.”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47750,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or in hot tea, which will melt a cold ice\ncube until they reach a medium temperature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51970,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You never see tepid tea spontaneously generate\nan ice cube while heating up, even though"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56320,
    "dDurationMs": 1829,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the total energy would be the same."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58149,
    "dDurationMs": 5171,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, useful energy is low entropy, out-of-equilibrium\nenergy that can be put to work, to turn a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63320,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "turbine or push a piston or melt an ice cube."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66420,
    "dDurationMs": 2329,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Useless energy, meanwhile, can’t be put\nto work."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68749,
    "dDurationMs": 4550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s out there in the form of waste heat\nor noise or the potential energy of a ball"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73299,
    "dDurationMs": 3221,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just sitting on the ground: we can't really\ndo anything with it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76520,
    "dDurationMs": 4009,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, gasoline and air carry useful,\nlow-entropy energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80529,
    "dDurationMs": 4171,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By burning them together, we can accelerate\na car, drive for a while, then put on the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84700,
    "dDurationMs": 1279,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "brakes and stop."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85979,
    "dDurationMs": 4841,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The total energy of the world remains constant\nduring the trip, but useful chemical energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90820,
    "dDurationMs": 3439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is converted into useless, high-entropy heat\nand noise."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94259,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The energy is still there, but we can't reclaim\nit to power any more cars, as convenient as"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99119,
    "dDurationMs": 1011,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that would be."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100130,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And thus it is with the earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101420,
    "dDurationMs": 5549,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The sun sends us energy in a convenient, useful,\nlow-entropy form, mainly as photons of visible"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106969,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107969,
    "dDurationMs": 4390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This energy gets absorbed and used and degraded\nby various processes here on Earth, until"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112359,
    "dDurationMs": 5370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we radiate it away in a much higher-entropy\nform: lots of infrared photons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117729,
    "dDurationMs": 5221,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For every visible photon we receive, the Earth\nradiates about twenty infrared photons out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122950,
    "dDurationMs": 1159,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124109,
    "dDurationMs": 3930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even though there’s a balance of energy\nin with energy out, the entropy of the energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128039,
    "dDurationMs": 2151,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has gone up twenty times."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130190,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Sun, in fact, is only a source of useful\nenergy because it's a hot, bright spot in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134670,
    "dDurationMs": 1310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a cold, dark sky."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135980,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If the whole sky were the temperature of the\nSun, our planet would receive a lot more energy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140200,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the Earth would quickly average out to\na state of high-entropy equilibrium, with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144250,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "everything at the temperature of the Sun."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146210,
    "dDurationMs": 3970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So things like driving or living would be\nimpossible – not because there’s insufficient"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150180,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "energy, but because you can’t do anything\nwhen all the energy has averaged out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154300,
    "dDurationMs": 6170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In equilibrium, all energy is equally useless,\nnothing ever changes, and time's arrow ceases"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160470,
    "dDurationMs": 2489,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to have any meaning."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162959,
    "dDurationMs": 3191,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey, Henry here, thanks for watching."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166150,
    "dDurationMs": 3789,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the fourth video in a series about\ntime and entropy made in collaboration with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169939,
    "dDurationMs": 1201,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "physicist Sean Carroll."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171140,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The series is supported with funding from\nGoogle’s Making and Science initiative,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174980,
    "dDurationMs": 3670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which seeks to encourage more young people\n(and people of all ages) to learn about and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178650,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fall in love with science and the world around\nthem, and the videos are based off of Sean’s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182530,
    "dDurationMs": 3770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "book “The Big Picture: On the Origins of\nLife, Meaning, and the Universe Itself,”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186300,
    "dDurationMs": 4979,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which you can find online or in bookstores\naround the world."
    } ]
  } ]
}
